zation.\n- Rich text formatting or media attachments.\n- Horizontal scaling across multiple server instances (PGLite is tied to the single Node instance).\n\n## Decisions\n\n**Decision 1: Embedded PGLite vs External Postgres**\n- *Rationale*: PGLite allows us to run PostgreSQL directly inside the Node.js process. This means users don't need to install or configure a separate database service. It seamlessly handles raw SQL queries and can persist to the filesystem.\n\n**Decision 2: Server-Sent Events (SSE) vs WebSockets**\n- *Rationale*: We only need one-way real-time communication (Server pushing new messages to Clients). Clients can post new messages via standard HTTP POST requests. SSE is much simpler to implement, works natively over standard HTTP, and doesn't require a complex WebSocket library like Socket.io.\n\n**Decision 3: Vanilla JS / Vite vs React**\n- *Rationale*: Given the minimal UI requirements (a message list and a text input), Vanilla JS keeps the build extremely fast and the dependency tree small. Vite provides a great developer experience out of the box.\n\n## Risks / Trade-offs\n\n- [Risk] PGLite performance on very large datasets: Embedded WASM databases are incredibly fast but might struggle if the dataset grows to tens of gigabytes.\n  - *Mitigation*: This is a local application and we expect message volume to be manageable for a single server instance.\n- [Risk] SSE connection limits: Browsers have limits on the number of concurrent SSE connections per domain.\n  - *Mitigation*: We only need one SSE connection per client tab, which is well within browser limits.\n\n## Why\n\nWe need a fast, local-first collaborative message board that allows users to post messages and see updates in real-time. This provides an incredibly low-latency experience by keeping data local while ensuring all users see the same state instantly. It serves as an excellent demonstration of using embedded PGLite combined with Server-Sent Events (SSE) to create a robust, lightweight realtime application without external database dependencies.\n\n## What Changes\n\n- We are introducing a brand new traditional client-server web application.\n- The backend will be a Node.js server using an embedded PGLite database for raw SQL queries, persisting data to the local disk.\n- Real-time synchronization will be handled via Server-Sent Events (SSE).\n- The frontend will be a simple, lightweight Single Page Application (Vanilla JS or React via Vite).\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### New Capabilities\n- `realtime-board`: The core message board capability covering posting messages, viewing a message feed, and receiving live updates via SSE.\n\n### Modified Capabilities\nNone (Greenfield project).\n\n## Impact\n\nThis is a brand new project. It will establish the foundational architecture including the Node.js backend setup, the embedded PGLite database structure, the SSE connection handling, and the frontend web UI.\n\n## 1. Project Initialization\n\n- [ ] 1.1 Initialize the Node.js project and install backend dependencies (express, @electric-sql/pglite, cors)\n- [ ] 1.2 Initialize the Vanilla JS / Vite project for the frontend and install frontend dependencies\n- [ ] 1.3 Set up basic npm scripts for concurrently running backend and frontend development servers\n- [ ] 1.4 Make the app start from a fresh checkout with no manual steps: once the dependencies declared in its package.json files are installed, `npm run dev` at the project root starts both the backend and the frontend, the backend creates any directory it needs (such as PGLite's data directory), and the page the frontend serves reaches the backend's API and event stream\n\n## 2. Backend Infrastructure & Database\n\n- [ ] 2.1 Set up a basic Express server with CORS and JSON body parsing\n- [ ] 2.2 Initialize embedded PGLite configured to write to the local file system\n- [ ] 2.3 Create the database initialization script (create `messages` table with `id`, `text`, `created_at`)\n- [ ] 2.4 Create the historical messages endpoint (`GET /api/messages`) to fetch initial state\n\n## 3. Real-time Capabilities (SSE)\n\n- [ ] 3.1 Implement the SSE endpoint (`GET /api/stream`) that maintains active connections with clients\n- [ ] 3.2 Implement the messaging endpoint (`POST /api/messages`) to insert text into PGLite\n- [ ] 3.3 Broadcast new messages to all active SSE connections when a new message is successfully inserted\n\n## 4. Frontend Implementation\n\n- [ ] 4.1 Create the basic HTML layout containing a message list and a text input form\n- [ ] 4.2 Fetch the message history (`GET /api/messages`) on initial page load and render messages\n- [ ] 4.3 Connect to the SSE endpoint (`GET /api/stream`) using `EventSource` to listen for new messages\n- [ ] 4.4 Append incoming real-time messages to the DOM seamlessly\n- [ ] 4.5 Wire up the form submission to send a `POST` request to `/api/messages` and clear the input<turn|>\n<|turn>model\n<|tool_call>call:list_dir{path:<|\"|>.<|\"|>}<tool_call|><|tool_response>response:list_dir{value:<|\"|>(empty)<|\"|>}<tool_response|><|tool_call>call:write_file{content:<|\"|>{\n  \"name\": \"realtime-message-board\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"concurrently \\\"npm run dev:backend\\\" \\\"npm run dev:frontend\\\"\",\n    \"dev:backend\": \"npm run dev --prefix backend\",\n    \"dev:frontend\": \"npm run dev --prefix frontend\",\n    \"install-all\": \"npm install && npm install --prefix backend && npm install --prefix frontend\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"concurrently\": \"^8.2.2\"\n  }\n}\n<|\"|>,path:<|\"|>package.json<|\"|>}<tool_call|><|tool_response>response:write_file{value:<|\"|>wrote 435 chars to package.json<|\"|>}<tool_response|><|tool_call>call:list_dir{path:<|\"|>.<|\"|>}<tool_call|><|tool_response>response:list_dir{value:<|\"|>package.json<|\"|>}<tool_response|><|tool_call>call:list_dir{path:<|\"|>/tmp/runs/smokes/gemma-moe-q4/message-board/no_verification/runs/101/app<|\"|>}<tool_call|><|tool_response>response:list_dir{value:<|\"|>package.json<|\"|>}<tool_response|><|tool_call>call:write_file{content:<|\"|>{\n  \"name\": \"backend\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"main\": \"index.js\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"start\": \"node index.js\",\n    \"dev\": \"node --watch index.js\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@electric-sql/pglite\": \"^0.2.0\",\n    \"cors\": \"^2.8.5\",\n    \"express\": \"^4.19.2\"\n  }\n}\n<|\"|>,path:<|\"|>backend/package.json<|\"|>}<tool_call|><|tool_response>response:write_file{value:<|\"|>wrote 283 chars to backend/package.json<|\"|>}<tool_response|><|tool_call>call:write_file{content:<|\"|>{\n  \"name\": \"frontend\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"vite\",\n    \"build\": \"vite build\",\n    \"preview\": \"vite preview\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {},\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"vite\": \"^5.2.0\"\n  }\n}\n<|\"|>,path:<|\"|>frontend/package.json<|\"|>}<tool_call|><|tool_response>response:write_file{value:<|\"|>wrote 253 chars to frontend/package.json<|\"|>}<tool_response|><|tool_call>call:write_file{content:<|\"|>import express from 'express';\nimport cors from 'cors';\nimport { PGLite } from '@electric-sql/pglite';\nimport path from 'path';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'url';\nimport fs from 'fs';\n\nconst __filename = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url);\nconst __dirname = path.dirname(__filename);\n\nconst app = express();\nconst port = 3001;\n\napp.use(cors());\napp.use(express.json());\n\n// Initialize PGLite with local filesystem persistence\nconst dbDir = path.join(__dirname, 'data');\nif (!fs.existsSync(dbDir)) {\n  fs.mkdirSync(dbDir);\n}\nconst db = new PGLite(dbDir);\n\n// SSE clients management\nlet clients = [];\n\n// Initialize Database\nasync function initDb() {\n  await db.exec(`\n    CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS messages (\n      id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,\n      text TEXT NOT NULL,\n      created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n    );\n  `);\n  console.log('Database initialized');\n}\n\ninitDb().catch(err => {\n  console.error('Failed to initialize database:', err);\n  process.exit(1);\n});\n\n// GET /api/messages - Fetch historical messages\napp.get('/api/messages', async (req, res) => {\n  try {\n    const result = await db.query('SELECT * FROM messages ORDER BY created_at ASC');\n    res.json(result.rows);\n  } catch (err) {\n    console.error(err);\n    res.status(500).send('Error fetching messages');\n  }\n});\n\n// POST /api/messages - Post a new message\napp.post('/api/messages', async (req, res) => {\n  const { text } = req.body;\n  if (!text) {\n    return res.status(400).send('Text is required');\n  }\n\n  try {\n    const result = await db.query(\n      'INSERT INTO messages (text) VALUES ($1) RETURNING *',\n      [text]\n    );\n    const newMessage = result.rows[0];\n\n    // Broadcast to SSE clients\n    clients.forEach(client => {\n      client.write(`data: ${JSON.stringify(newMessage)}\\n\\n`);\n    });\n\n    res.status(201).json(newMessage);\n  } catch (err) {\n    console.error(err);\n    res.status(500).send('Error saving message');\n  }\n});\n\n// GET /api/stream - SSE endpoint\napp.get('/api/stream', (req, res) => {\n  res.setHeader('Content-Type', 'text/event-stream');\n  res.setHeader('Cache-Control', 'no-cache');\n  res.setHeader('Connection', 'keep-alive');\n\n  const client = res;\n  clients.push(client);\n\n  req.on('close', () => {\n    clients = clients.filter(c => c!== client);\n  });\n});\n\napp.listen(port, () => {\n  console.log(`Backend listening at http://localhost:${port}`);\n});\n<|\"|>,path:<|\"|>backend/index.js<|\"|>}<tool_call|><|tool_response>response:write_file{value:<|\"|>wrote 2386 chars to backend/index.js<|\"|>}<tool_response|><|tool_call>call:write_file{content:<|\"|>import { createApp } from '/src/app.js';\n\n// For simplicity in this environment, we'll just run it directly\n// In a real Vite app, this would be handled by the build/dev process\ncreateApp();\n<|\"|>,path:<|\"|>frontend/index.html<|\"|>}<tool_call|><|tool_response>response:write_file{value:<|\"|>wrote 191 chars to frontend/index.html<|\"|>}<tool_response|><|tool_call>call:write_file{content:<|\"|><!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Realtime Message Board</title>\n    <style>\n        body {\n            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\n            max-width: 600px;\n            margin: 2rem auto;\n            padding: 0 1rem;\n            display: flex;\n            flex-direction: column;\n            height: 90vh;\n        }\n        #message-list {\n            flex-grow: 1;\n            overflow-y: auto;\n            border: 1px solid #ccc;\n            padding: 1rem;\n            margin-bottom: 1rem;\n            border-radius: 4px;\n            display: flex;\n            flex-direction: column;\n            gap: 0.5rem;\n        }\n       .message {\n            padding: 0.5rem;\n            background: #f4f4f4;\n            border-radius: 4px;\n            word-break: break-word;\n        }\n       .message.timestamp {\n            font-size: 0.75rem;\n            color: #666;\n            margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n        }\n        #message-form {\n            display: flex;\n            gap: 0.5rem;\n        }\n        #message-input {\n            flex-grow: 1;\n            padding: 0.5rem;\n            border: 1px solid #ccc;\n            border-radius: 4px;\n        }\n        #submit-button {\n            padding: 0.5rem 1rem;\n            background: #007bff;\n            color: white;\n            border: none;\n            border-radius: 4px;\n            cursor: pointer;\n        }\n        #submit-button:hover {\n            background: #0056b3;\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <h1>Message Board</h1>\n    <div id=\"message-list\"></div>\n    <form id=\"message-form\">\n        <input type=\"text\" id=\"message-input\" placeholder=\"Type a message...\" required>\n        <button type=\"submit\" id=\"submit-button\">Send</button>\n    </form>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n<|\"|>,path:<|\"|>frontend/index.html<|\"|>}<tool_call|><|tool_response>response:write_file{value:<|\"|>wrote 1992 chars to frontend/index.html<|\"|>}<tool_response|><|tool_call>call:write_file{content:<|\"|>const API_BASE = 'http://localhost:3001/api';\n\nfunction createApp() {\n    const messageList = document.getElementById('message-list');\n    const messageForm = document.getElementById('message-form');\n    const messageInput = document.getElementById('message-input');\n\n    function appendMessage(message) {\n        const div = document.createElement('div');\n        div.className ='message';\n        \n        const timestamp = document.createElement('div');\n        timestamp.className = 'timestamp';\n        timestamp.textContent = new Date(message.created_at).toLocaleString();\n        \n        const text = document.createElement('div');\n        text.textContent = message.text;\n        \n        div.appendChild(timestamp);\n        div.appendChild(text);\n        messageList.appendChild(div);\n        \n        // Scroll to bottom\n        messageList.scrollTop = messageList.scrollHeight;\n    }\n\n    // Initial fetch\n    async function fetchMessages() {\n        try {\n            const response = await fetch(`${API_BASE}/messages`);\n            const messages = await response.json();\n            messageList.innerHTML = '';\n            messages.forEach(appendMessage);\n        } catch (err) {\n            console.error('Error fetching messages:', err);\n        }\n    }\n\n    // SSE Connection\n    function setupSSE() {\n        const eventSource = new EventSource(`${API_BASE}/stream`);\n        \n        eventSource.onmessage = (event) => {\n            const newMessage = JSON.parse(event.data);\n            appendMessage(newMessage);\n        };\n\n        eventSource.onerror = (err) => {\n            console.error('SSE Error:', err);\n            // EventSource will automatically try to reconnect, \n            // but we could handle it here if needed.\n        };\n    }\n\n    // Form handling\n    messageForm.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {\n        e.preventDefault();\n        const text = messageInput.value.trim();\n        if (!text) return;\n\n        messageInput.value = '';\n\n        try {\n            const response = await fetch(`${API_BASE}/messages`, {\n                method: 'POST',\n                headers: {\n                    'Content-Type': 'application/json'\n                },\n                body: JSON.stringify({ text })\n            });\n\n            if (!response.ok) {\n                throw new Error('Failed to post message');\n            }\n        } catch (err) {\n            console.error('Error posting message:', err);\n            alert('Failed to send message');\n        }\n    });\n\n    fetchMessages();\n    setupSSE();\n}\n\n// Export for use in index.html if needed, although we're using type=\"module\"\nif (typeof module!== 'undefined') {\n    module.exports = { createApp };\n} else {\n    // In the browser\n    window.createApp = createApp;\n}\n<|\"|>,path:<|\"|>frontend/src/main.js<|\"|>}<tool_call|><|tool_response>response:write_file{value:<|\"|>wrote 2777 chars to frontend/src/main.js<|\"|>}<tool_response|>","generated":""}
